reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/probe-review.jsonl:7:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PEvJmoBsVwRS6nsozZbc3w","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Step 2 score experiment — design for review\n2\t\n3\tAlex asks whether sending embedding similarity to Jev helps, given existing high retrieval recall and merge quality. This is an isolated fixed-history diagnostic, not a product change, adoption, a fresh held-out acceptance, or a comparison of search recall. Prior recorded acceptance 141/143 is search recall, 1/57 clearly wrong merges is not recall of Jev's repeat decisions. The fresh frozen reference and old labels do not change. Start with 10 archived c8 fresh comparison requests, selected before sending, covering the clearly wrong merge, disputed overlaps, accepted repeats, and new-evidence controls: `22:ev-11`, `13:e11`, `38:ev-2`, `18:e2`, `43:e3`, `3:e1`, `9:e6`, `14:e3`, `5:e1`, `9:e1`. Three arms times three draws = 90 calls, with the original candidate sets and state fixed. This is a selected diagnostic and cannot measure overall precision or recall. A larger comparison is considered only if the cheap probe reveals a useful signal (AGENTS §7.3); the raw articles are already used, so neither probe is fresh acceptance.\n4\t\n5\t## What is sent and why\n6\t\n7\tC control: exact archived model/state/questions. T: each candidate instruction adds factual metadata: `Retrieval cosine similarities (query-to-stored-text; not a probability): query 1: 0.xxxx; query 2: ...`. Each query corresponds in order to the existing caller's query_vectors; its label and query type are made explicit without disclosing thesis text otherwise not sent. Include a score for each query, including non-retrieving queries, and the origin query. P placebo: same text and query types, but scores permuted across candidates per query with deterministic seed. This tests numeric signal versus extra formatting but cannot distinguish all model sensitivity from distractors, and one-candidate or equal-valued score requests cannot be perturbed. Freeze this representation; do not infer importance from cosine or set thresholds. Decimal precision 4, cosine computed with existing compare.py and cached exact text vectors. Retrieval always uses original queries, no candidate changes, shuffle does not change selection. User requests testing this candidate, not deployment or any new rule.\n8\t\n9\t## State × event\n10\t\n11\t| Event | State and action | Date/time |\n12\t|---|---|---|\n13\t| Preflight | Read archives read-only; rebuild all 185 request bytes and answers; compare identity and score reconstruction. Abort on missing keys, candidates, requests or inconsistent data. | No wall-clock data in requests |\n14\t| First send | Separate research archive for each arm/draw; interleave all 9 requests per case in fixed seeded order; fresh transport, no archived cache hit. | Same day for all arms; timestamps metadata only |\n15\t| Transport failure | Record actual error; bounded underlying transport retry; incomplete case remains failed, no replacement or analysis as different. | No date decision |\n16\t| Crash or interruption | Durable per-arm archive; no unrecorded retry; resume only missing planned requests, preserving planned ordering where possible; disclose interruption/time. | Save identifiers, not wall-clock ordering |\n17\t| Completed response | Validate with current Jev validator; record raw response and costs; malformed/refusal stops case and is reported. | Original dates stay unchanged |\n18\t| Analysis | Compare each request on fixed original library; no advance to newly grouped state; reviewed changes and controls with source, not self-scorer claims. | Historical source dates preserved |\n19\t| Later run/config change/another writer/two scopes | Refuse existing output on rerun absent exact frozen manifest and explicit resume; do not access live data or concurrent Step 1 writes. Different scopes use different research directories and archives. | No runtime time used as identity |\n20\t\n21\t## Values × readers\n22\t\n23\t| Value | Origin | Reader | Consequence |\n24\t|---|---|---|---|\n25\t| query and record text | saved Step 1 trace | existing query construction, Jev | Preserve bytes and record identity |\n26\t| query-to-group cosine | cached embeddings and current cosine | T Jev question only; P shuffled | Keep query provenance; numeric score is not truth |\n27\t| Jev choice/probabilities | model per candidate | original outcome function | Compare same candidate ids and code; no probability gate |\n28\t| group outcome | original outcome | read-only analysis and blind readers | Compare mergers, target group, revisions and omissions, including changed outcomes and controls |\n29\t| article and source | archived Step 1 input | independent blind reader | Judge whether actual statements are same, revised, or different; no score/arm/model decision shown |\n30\t| cost/failure | archives | report | Never infer zero from missing response |\n31\t\n32\t## New path × old checks\n33\t\n34\t| Check | C | T/P |\n35\t|---|---|---|\n36\t| model, state, candidate order, choice criteria | exact archive equality | identical, only question text lines appended |\n37\t| request JSON identity | equal per archived request | first strip appended metadata, equals original |\n38\t| score alignment | not sent | raw values recomputed against exact query and candidate; permutation checked within query |\n39\t| Jev choice set and probability validation | current validator | same validator |\n40\t| missing input / empty population | refuse | refuse |\n41\t| stored historical answers | replay baseline 185 exact requests/answers without live calls | original answer passes current validator |\n42\t| outcome function | original candidates and order | same; group state frozen |\n43\t| unrelated later-link Jev calls | excluded | excluded |\n44\t\n45\t## Acceptance and analysis\n46\t\n47\t1. Report every request, candidate, transport failure, cost and baseline variability. Quantify disagreements C vs T vs P and change in wrong merges, missed repeats, revisions and target group, paired by request and draw. Score-sensitivity is not proof of accuracy. No search recall improvement can be attributed to this intervention because search is held fixed.\n48\t2. As Jev and saved references are incomplete, blind readers inspect all cases with changed outcomes and a predeclared random set of unchanged controls, including all known wrong merges and known-repeat candidates, against original sources. Mixed arms shown without scores, arm labels, candidate rank or model decision. Two independent reviews and adjudication of disagreements; do not use a new score program as semantic judge. If workload exceeds available reviewer context, partition into bounded batches and report coverage.\n49\t3. Prior fresh acceptance includes no observed revisions: do not claim revision quality. A separate case set of documented real revisions may be read and assessed; it cannot stand in for the full product path.\n50\t4. One draw can expose mechanism; 3 same-day control draws characterize instability, not guarantee statistical power. State the counts and losses; no unregistered win threshold. Effect would justify a later separately approved, forward full-path validation; no effect is not proof of equivalence. Predeclare a compact decision before send with council, not after output.\n51\t\n52\t## Prior decisions and limits\n53\t\n54\tD381 selects the candidate with highest Jev same-statement probability; this experiment retains it. D379 seals old product; no frozen files or production config touched. AGENTS §7.1 historical rulers unchanged; repeat reference is exploratory, not new frozen gold. AGENTS §7.2 read raw answer against source. Current Jev model `jev-1.14.0`. Offline census reconstructs and verifies all 185 comparison requests and answers. Standing preflight run against v108 archive judged 243 extraction answers and 170 matching records, two matching records skipped, 12 extraction records dropped and 2 stored schema refusals; that script does not test the clean Jev score path. The latter needs its own replay and refusal controls before send.\n55\t\n56\t## Probe prediction and stop\n57\t\n58\tHypothesis: score information moves at least one relevant comparison beyond the change caused by a shuffled number and makes at least one source-backed decision better without a source-backed decision getting worse. Prediction: the clearly wrong X22 grouping becomes separate more often in T than C, while the selected accepted-repeat controls remain correctly grouped. We do not predict a perfect result. Predeclare individual decision comparisons, 3 samples per arm and show all 90 outcomes and errors. If T fails to improve any inspected decision, or causes a material wrong merge or loses a valid repeat without a balancing demonstrated gain, stop this line and report; no full experiment follows automatically. If a decisive contrast is absent or conflicting, report inconclusive. This is a heuristic stop on the selected probe, not a quantitative estimate of product impact. Blind-read every differing case plus each selected known-merge reference and at least two unchanged controls, including all original source material. Register case ids and score mapping before any send; send no paid calls until council review and preflight pass.\n59\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c06c24f-8f77-4add-9443-7081a27b7903","uuid":"00a4b582-dd3b-493c-a842-232666a2667d","timestamp":"2026-11-09T01:23:15.129Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/EXPERIMENT-DESIGN.md","content":"# Step 2 score experiment — design for review\n\nAlex asks whether sending embedding similarity to Jev helps, given existing high retrieval recall and merge quality. This is an isolated fixed-history diagnostic, not a product change, adoption, a fresh held-out acceptance, or a comparison of search recall. Prior recorded acceptance 141/143 is search recall, 1/57 clearly wrong merges is not recall of Jev's repeat decisions. The fresh frozen reference and old labels do not change. Start with 10 archived c8 fresh comparison requests, selected before sending, covering the clearly wrong merge, disputed overlaps, accepted repeats, and new-evidence controls: `22:ev-11`, `13:e11`, `38:ev-2`, `18:e2`, `43:e3`, `3:e1`, `9:e6`, `14:e3`, `5:e1`, `9:e1`. Three arms times three draws = 90 calls, with the original candidate sets and state fixed. This is a selected diagnostic and cannot measure overall precision or recall. A larger comparison is considered only if the cheap probe reveals a useful signal (AGENTS §7.3); the raw articles are already used, so neither probe is fresh acceptance.\n\n## What is sent and why\n\nC control: exact archived model/state/questions. T: each candidate instruction adds factual metadata: `Retrieval cosine similarities (query-to-stored-text; not a probability): query 1: 0.xxxx; query 2: ...`. Each query corresponds in order to the existing caller's query_vectors; its label and query type are made explicit without disclosing thesis text otherwise not sent. Include a score for each query, including non-retrieving queries, and the origin query. P placebo: same text and query types, but scores permuted across candidates per query with deterministic seed. This tests numeric signal versus extra formatting but cannot distinguish all model sensitivity from distractors, and one-candidate or equal-valued score requests cannot be perturbed. Freeze this representation; do not infer importance from cosine or set thresholds. Decimal precision 4, cosine computed with existing compare.py and cached exact text vectors. Retrieval always uses original queries, no candidate changes, shuffle does not change selection. User requests testing this candidate, not deployment or any new rule.\n\n## State × event\n\n| Event | State and action | Date/time |\n|---|---|---|\n| Preflight | Read archives read-only; rebuild all 185 request bytes and answers; compare identity and score reconstruction. Abort on missing keys, candidates, requests or inconsistent data. | No wall-clock data in requests |\n| First send | Separate research archive for each arm/draw; interleave all 9 requests per case in fixed seeded order; fresh transport, no archived cache hit. | Same day for all arms; timestamps metadata only |\n| Transport failure | Record actual error; bounded underlying transport retry; incomplete case remains failed, no replacement or analysis as different. | No date decision |\n| Crash or interruption | Durable per-arm archive; no unrecorded retry; resume only missing planned requests, preserving planned ordering where possible; disclose interruption/time. | Save identifiers, not wall-clock ordering |\n| Completed response | Validate with current Jev validator; record raw response and costs; malformed/refusal stops case and is reported. | Original dates stay unchanged |\n| Analysis | Compare each request on fixed original library; no advance to newly grouped state; reviewed changes and controls with source, not self-scorer claims. | Historical source dates preserved |\n| Later run/config change/another writer/two scopes | Refuse existing output on rerun absent exact frozen manifest and explicit resume; do not access live data or concurrent Step 1 writes. Different scopes use different research directories and archives. | No runtime time used as identity |\n\n## Values × readers\n\n| Value | Origin | Reader | Consequence |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| query and record text | saved Step 1 trace | existing query construction, Jev | Preserve bytes and record identity |\n| query-to-group cosine | cached embeddings and current cosine | T Jev question only; P shuffled | Keep query provenance; numeric score is not truth |\n| Jev choice/probabilities | model per candidate | original outcome function | Compare same candidate ids and code; no probability gate |\n| group outcome | original outcome | read-only analysis and blind readers | Compare mergers, target group, revisions and omissions, including changed outcomes and controls |\n| article and source | archived Step 1 input | independent blind reader | Judge whether actual statements are same, revised, or different; no score/arm/model decision shown |\n| cost/failure | archives | report | Never infer zero from missing response |\n\n## New path × old checks\n\n| Check | C | T/P |\n|---|---|---|\n| model, state, candidate order, choice criteria | exact archive equality | identical, only question text lines appended |\n| request JSON identity | equal per archived request | first strip appended metadata, equals original |\n| score alignment | not sent | raw values recomputed against exact query and candidate; permutation checked within query |\n| Jev choice set and probability validation | current validator | same validator |\n| missing input / empty population | refuse | refuse |\n| stored historical answers | replay baseline 185 exact requests/answers without live calls | original answer passes current validator |\n| outcome function | original candidates and order | same; group state frozen |\n| unrelated later-link Jev calls | excluded | excluded |\n\n## Acceptance and analysis\n\n1. Report every request, candidate, transport failure, cost and baseline variability. Quantify disagreements C vs T vs P and change in wrong merges, missed repeats, revisions and target group, paired by request and draw. Score-sensitivity is not proof of accuracy. No search recall improvement can be attributed to this intervention because search is held fixed.\n2. As Jev and saved references are incomplete, blind readers inspect all cases with changed outcomes and a predeclared random set of unchanged controls, including all known wrong merges and known-repeat candidates, against original sources. Mixed arms shown without scores, arm labels, candidate rank or model decision. Two independent reviews and adjudication of disagreements; do not use a new score program as semantic judge. If workload exceeds available reviewer context, partition into bounded batches and report coverage.\n3. Prior fresh acceptance includes no observed revisions: do not claim revision quality. A separate case set of documented real revisions may be read and assessed; it cannot stand in for the full product path.\n4. One draw can expose mechanism; 3 same-day control draws characterize instability, not guarantee statistical power. State the counts and losses; no unregistered win threshold. Effect would justify a later separately approved, forward full-path validation; no effect is not proof of equivalence. Predeclare a compact decision before send with council, not after output.\n\n## Prior decisions and limits\n\nD381 selects the candidate with highest Jev same-statement probability; this experiment retains it. D379 seals old product; no frozen files or production config touched. AGENTS §7.1 historical rulers unchanged; repeat reference is exploratory, not new frozen gold. AGENTS §7.2 read raw answer against source. Current Jev model `jev-1.14.0`. Offline census reconstructs and verifies all 185 comparison requests and answers. Standing preflight run against v108 archive judged 243 extraction answers and 170 matching records, two matching records skipped, 12 extraction records dropped and 2 stored schema refusals; that script does not test the clean Jev score path. The latter needs its own replay and refusal controls before send.\n\n## Probe prediction and stop\n\nHypothesis: score information moves at least one relevant comparison beyond the change caused by a shuffled number and makes at least one source-backed decision better without a source-backed decision getting worse. Prediction: the clearly wrong X22 grouping becomes separate more often in T than C, while the selected accepted-repeat controls remain correctly grouped. We do not predict a perfect result. Predeclare individual decision comparisons, 3 samples per arm and show all 90 outcomes and errors. If T fails to improve any inspected decision, or causes a material wrong merge or loses a valid repeat without a balancing demonstrated gain, stop this line and report; no full experiment follows automatically. If a decisive contrast is absent or conflicting, report inconclusive. This is a heuristic stop on the selected probe, not a quantitative estimate of product impact. Blind-read every differing case plus each selected known-merge reference and at least two unchanged controls, including all original source material. Register case ids and score mapping before any send; send no paid calls until council review and preflight pass.\n","numLines":59,"startLine":1,"totalLines":59}}}
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/probe-review.jsonl:15:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UEZyJPGFU23YfD8eDkZmTK","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Step 2: should Jev see retrieval scores?\n2\t\n3\tResearch council, 2026-11-08. Scope: the isolated clean Step 2 evidence-comparison path. No production change, model test, or change to the concurrent Step 1 experiment.\n4\t\n5\t## Conclusion\n6\t\n7\tNeither a benefit nor harm has been established. Keep the present request until a controlled comparison shows an advantage. Similarity is calculated between a search query and a stored group's original text; it is not a probability of same statement. The query may contain a thesis and a candidate may have several scores from different queries. Jev does not receive these scores; it receives the incoming piece as state and one candidate per typed question. It returns a choice and probabilities. Jev's choice probability, not cosine, selects among multiple same-statement results.\n8\t\n9\t## Concrete observation\n10\t\n11\tIn saved c6 X4, incoming 12:e1 was grouped into 1:E1 although the two revenue-sharing arrangements were judged different. Recomputed from the cached exact-text vectors, cosine of the one thesis query against 1:E1's document is 0.8574. Its own document-vector cosine is 0.8654, but the record had one thesis query and that value was not its retrieval query. The saved Jev answer called same_statement at 0.89. This is one error; it neither establishes that score information will harm Jev nor measures a score distribution. Source: `poc/data/clean-step2-forward-c6-2026-11-08/{decisions.json,library.json,embeddings.json,merge-key.json,merge-third-answer.json}`. Query/doc text and cosine are reconstructed as `clean-arch/step2/compare.py` defines them.\n12\t\n13\t## Council\n14\t\n15\tClaude Code session 4c06c24f-8f77-4add-9443-7081a27b7903; original handoff, streams, stderr and challenge are saved alongside this record. Claude initially recommended an offline score-separation gate. Codex challenged it: overlapping marginal scores cannot rule out conditional help, and separation cannot establish Jev uses them. Claude agreed and withdrew that gate, its extrapolation of score ranges from another task, and claims about Jev's internal reasoning. Offline profiling can inform a test but cannot establish efficacy. Vendor describes Jev as a typed, non-text-generating decision model with independently evaluated questions (https://docs.typesafe.ai/introduction); evidence on LLM anchoring is only a hypothesis for Jev, not a finding (https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.01724).\n16\t\n17\t## Proposed discriminating test, not yet registered or run\n18\t\n19\tReconstruct identical saved candidate requests; interleave fresh no-score controls with true-score requests and a score-shuffled control, with fixed score representation and randomization, repeated draws, cache misses, and identical model, candidates and question content except score lines. Make each score's query origin explicit: multiple search queries may yield different scores. A shuffled control tests sensitivity to a number but needs care with singleton/equal-score cases and preserving query origin. A source-blind independent reader judges differing pairs and controls without seeing arm, score, or prior decision. Report wrong merges, missed repeats, incorrect revision classifications and group choices separately, all cases, with same-arm variability, cost and limitations; fixed-candidate comparisons do not prove forward-run performance. The fresh set has few or no revisions; use separately identified stored revision cases without presenting isolated pair results as product-path evidence. Freeze design, audit and preflight under repository rules before any paid send. A score can also encode context Jev did not directly receive (e.g. thesis wording or period), so improvement would not itself establish the mechanism.\n20\t\n21\tNo evidence supports a universal score threshold. This proposal does not alter the accepted configuration or authorize deployment.\n22\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c06c24f-8f77-4add-9443-7081a27b7903","uuid":"e523ecf3-62ca-440c-a6b4-c93f2ecc027e","timestamp":"2026-11-09T01:23:23.861Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/CONCLUSIONS.md","content":"# Step 2: should Jev see retrieval scores?\n\nResearch council, 2026-11-08. Scope: the isolated clean Step 2 evidence-comparison path. No production change, model test, or change to the concurrent Step 1 experiment.\n\n## Conclusion\n\nNeither a benefit nor harm has been established. Keep the present request until a controlled comparison shows an advantage. Similarity is calculated between a search query and a stored group's original text; it is not a probability of same statement. The query may contain a thesis and a candidate may have several scores from different queries. Jev does not receive these scores; it receives the incoming piece as state and one candidate per typed question. It returns a choice and probabilities. Jev's choice probability, not cosine, selects among multiple same-statement results.\n\n## Concrete observation\n\nIn saved c6 X4, incoming 12:e1 was grouped into 1:E1 although the two revenue-sharing arrangements were judged different. Recomputed from the cached exact-text vectors, cosine of the one thesis query against 1:E1's document is 0.8574. Its own document-vector cosine is 0.8654, but the record had one thesis query and that value was not its retrieval query. The saved Jev answer called same_statement at 0.89. This is one error; it neither establishes that score information will harm Jev nor measures a score distribution. Source: `poc/data/clean-step2-forward-c6-2026-11-08/{decisions.json,library.json,embeddings.json,merge-key.json,merge-third-answer.json}`. Query/doc text and cosine are reconstructed as `clean-arch/step2/compare.py` defines them.\n\n## Council\n\nClaude Code session 4c06c24f-8f77-4add-9443-7081a27b7903; original handoff, streams, stderr and challenge are saved alongside this record. Claude initially recommended an offline score-separation gate. Codex challenged it: overlapping marginal scores cannot rule out conditional help, and separation cannot establish Jev uses them. Claude agreed and withdrew that gate, its extrapolation of score ranges from another task, and claims about Jev's internal reasoning. Offline profiling can inform a test but cannot establish efficacy. Vendor describes Jev as a typed, non-text-generating decision model with independently evaluated questions (https://docs.typesafe.ai/introduction); evidence on LLM anchoring is only a hypothesis for Jev, not a finding (https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.01724).\n\n## Proposed discriminating test, not yet registered or run\n\nReconstruct identical saved candidate requests; interleave fresh no-score controls with true-score requests and a score-shuffled control, with fixed score representation and randomization, repeated draws, cache misses, and identical model, candidates and question content except score lines. Make each score's query origin explicit: multiple search queries may yield different scores. A shuffled control tests sensitivity to a number but needs care with singleton/equal-score cases and preserving query origin. A source-blind independent reader judges differing pairs and controls without seeing arm, score, or prior decision. Report wrong merges, missed repeats, incorrect revision classifications and group choices separately, all cases, with same-arm variability, cost and limitations; fixed-candidate comparisons do not prove forward-run performance. The fresh set has few or no revisions; use separately identified stored revision cases without presenting isolated pair results as product-path evidence. Freeze design, audit and preflight under repository rules before any paid send. A score can also encode context Jev did not directly receive (e.g. thesis wording or period), so improvement would not itself establish the mechanism.\n\nNo evidence supports a universal score threshold. This proposal does not alter the accepted configuration or authorize deployment.\n","numLines":22,"startLine":1,"totalLines":22}}}
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/probe-review.jsonl:32:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrUt4Sy9xQGkBA2KmRr1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VYDsCpYa46pYxReHZaNfZQ","name":"Grep","input":{"pattern":"\"(22:ev-11|13:e11|38:ev-2|18:e2|43:e3|3:e1|9:e6|14:e3|5:e1|9:e1)\": \"","path":"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/library.json","output_mode":"content","-n":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4848,"cache_read_input_tokens":324211,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4848},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c06c24f-8f77-4add-9443-7081a27b7903","uuid":"4aa467a3-148e-449b-b370-e5365c76ecb0","timestamp":"2026-11-09T01:24:51.926Z","request_id":"req_011CgrUt3vDa9iYoTgGijDpZ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01VYDsCpYa46pYxReHZaNfZQ":{"pattern":"\"(22:ev-11|13:e11|38:ev-2|18:e2|43:e3|3:e1|9:e6|14:e3|5:e1|9:e1)\": \"","path":"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/library.json","output_mode":"content","-n":true}}}
