reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/round-2.jsonl:101:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Frtgn33caRfda3Z28iBXTr","type":"tool_result","content":"1\tYou are an independent senior reader for a hedge-fund research system. Read-only task: do not edit files or run model calls.\n2\t\n3\tRead /Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/merge-third-packet.json. Do not open any other file. Each entry is a pair of evidence records about NVIDIA from two articles. The library has filed \"later\" in the group of \"earlier\" as a repeat: an analyst reading that group sees earlier's record first and later's own full text below it as a later report of the same statement.\n4\t\n5\tFor each entry, judge from the passages and context which applies:\n6\t- \"acceptable\": later reports earlier's main statement (extra detail or different wording allowed);\n7\t- \"overlap\": later's record contains earlier's statement but its own main point is broader or different, or the two describe the same fact with a materially different qualification (for example orders versus sales); filing it there is imperfect but an analyst reading later's own text would not be misled;\n8\t- \"wrong\": later's main statement is a different fact, figure, party, product or event, and filing it as a repeat of earlier would mislead an analyst.\n9\t\n10\tReturn only a JSON array in packet order: [{\"id\": \"X..\", \"merge_acceptable\": true|false, \"verdict\": \"acceptable\"|\"overlap\"|\"wrong\", \"why\": \"<one short sentence>\"}]. Set merge_acceptable true for acceptable, false otherwise.\n11\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c06c24f-8f77-4add-9443-7081a27b7903","uuid":"4894bfb8-3106-44a1-934e-d24738b92528","timestamp":"2026-11-09T01:02:39.751Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/merge-third-prompt.md","content":"You are an independent senior reader for a hedge-fund research system. Read-only task: do not edit files or run model calls.\n\nRead /Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/merge-third-packet.json. Do not open any other file. Each entry is a pair of evidence records about NVIDIA from two articles. The library has filed \"later\" in the group of \"earlier\" as a repeat: an analyst reading that group sees earlier's record first and later's own full text below it as a later report of the same statement.\n\nFor each entry, judge from the passages and context which applies:\n- \"acceptable\": later reports earlier's main statement (extra detail or different wording allowed);\n- \"overlap\": later's record contains earlier's statement but its own main point is broader or different, or the two describe the same fact with a materially different qualification (for example orders versus sales); filing it there is imperfect but an analyst reading later's own text would not be misled;\n- \"wrong\": later's main statement is a different fact, figure, party, product or event, and filing it as a repeat of earlier would mislead an analyst.\n\nReturn only a JSON array in packet order: [{\"id\": \"X..\", \"merge_acceptable\": true|false, \"verdict\": \"acceptable\"|\"overlap\"|\"wrong\", \"why\": \"<one short sentence>\"}]. Set merge_acceptable true for acceptable, false otherwise.\n","numLines":11,"startLine":1,"totalLines":11}}}
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/round-2.jsonl:214:{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrTL1AkhUpuBkuq6wz1W","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# 把 cosine 交给 Jev：自我挑战与逐条回应（只读）\n\n**修正后的结论：上一轮我把\"离线分数分析没有区分度\"当成\"不必发送\"的理由，这是错的。** 离线分析既证明不了没用，也证明不了 Jev 会用这个分数。能真正回答问题的最便宜检验，是把已存的 Jev 请求原样重发，分成三组对照：\n\n- **原样组**：请求一字不改；\n- **真分数组**：只在每个问题里加上真实的分数；\n- **打乱分数组**：同一请求内把分数在候选之间打乱后加上。\n\n只在验收集上做，估计花费不到 1 美元（这是估算）；真正的成本是读者的时间。它改动了 Jev 的输入，所以算一轮新改动：发送前要过 council，并由 Alex 决定是否开这一轮。当前排在第一的任务是 D388（`docs/CURRENT_STATE.md:123-125`）。\n\n---\n\n## 1. 对你每一条的回应\n\n| # | 你的观点 | 我的立场 | 理由与证据 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 分数的分布在两组之间重叠，Jev 照样可能受益（条件信息、交互作用）；单变量离线检验失败证明不了没好处；有区分度也证明不了 Jev 在用 | **同意，两半都同意** | 上一轮的\"A 步不通过就停\"不该当决策规则。补一个具体机制：分数里含有 Jev 现在看不到的信息。被向量化的文本 `doc_text` 里有 `evidence_period`，`query_text` 里有论点问题（`compare.py:31-37`），而 Jev 看到的 `piece_text` 两样都没有（`compare.py:40-42`）。所以\"条件信息\"在结构上确实存在。这也带来一个混杂因素：分数即使有用，也可能只是在替这两个字段传话，所以归因需要单独的对照（见第 3 节 X 组）。 |\n| 2a | \"0.4 已经算高、这个模型分数天然偏低\"来自另一个任务，不能推广 | **同意，撤回** | 依据 `search.py:27-30` 是 2026-10-24 在 74 句话上做的\"想法对观点\"任务，文本模板不同。我读过的所有文件里，都没有 Step 2 候选的分数分布。用缓存的向量可以零成本算出来，但现在没人算过。 |\n| 2b | 第 10 名的分数不一定高 | **同意，还要补一条** | `search()` 是把整个库排序后截前 10（`compare.py:104`）。前向运行的早期，库里不到 10 个组，所有组都会成为候选，和相似度无关。所以同一请求里分数的跨度，早期可能很大、后期可能很窄。这一点是读代码得出的；具体数值不知道。 |\n| 2c | 不知道 X4 的 cosine | **同意，撤回这个例子** | 我说\"它进前 10 正是因为 cosine 高\"是错的。进前 10 只说明它在当时的库里排名靠前，说明不了绝对数值。 |\n| 3 | 没发现 Step 2 的瓶颈、验收通过、1/57 贴近门槛，这些都不能说明影响，也不能说明可以上生产；数字有限 | **同意** | 我把两件事混在了一起。一件是排序：有没有一个正在失败的错误类型需要动手（AGENTS §1、§7.3）。另一件是分数本身有没有效果。前者说明不了后者。还要更正三处：(a) \"Search is not the bottleneck\"（`step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md:176`）说的是检索，不是比较；(b) 现有三条线都不测 Jev 漏判的重复；(c) 验收集里一个修订都没有（`clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2.log:2`，只有 new 和 repeat 两种结果），dev 每次也只有 2–3 个。1/57 的不确定性也很大：Clopper–Pearson 双侧 95% 上界约 9.4%（我的估算），所以\"达线\"只是点估计。\"只差一个合并\"说明的是这条线很脆弱，不是分数有害的证据。 |\n| 4 | 把 LLM 的锚定效应套到 Jev 上只是假设；Jev 不生成文字，是另一类东西；不能断言它不会推理、没有数字刻度 | **同意，撤回断言** | 能观察到的只有：它不返回文字，所以我们看不到它怎么推理。它内部会不会推理、能不能把数字当刻度来用，仓库里没有证据。厂商 1.13 版\"数字推理是弱项\"的说法，我是从 `codex-jev-usage-review.md:343` 二手转述的：版本是 1.13 不是 1.14，没有给数字，我也没读原页。\"分数会强化错误\"降级为三个并列假设之一：有帮助、有害、被忽略。 |\n| 5 | 离线分析有用，但不该当关卡；它的阴性结果算不算定论 | **同意：不是定论，也不当关卡** | AGENTS §1 第 4 步要求的\"最便宜的证明\"，原文就是\"a stored input edited and re-run\"，也就是改一个存储的输入再重发，而不是先做一次分数普查。离线分析的用处见第 4 节。 |\n\n**我仍然坚持、或者反过来挑战你的几点：**\n\n- **合并歧义是真实存在的（读代码证实）。** 一个候选对应几条查询就有几个分数（`compare.py:45-51`、`:103-105`）。给分数的规则必须在发送前登记好，否则真分数组本身就没有定义。\n- **只要改了 Jev 的输入，就是新的一轮。** 仓库里对另一处改动已经写过同样的原则：\"changing it changes measured Step 2 behaviour and needs its own measurement\"（`docs/CURRENT_STATE.md:37`）。加进去的那句话在判别标准里找不到出处，按 AGENTS §6 属于要交给 Alex 的提议。\n- **\"沿用同一套读者流程\"做不到完全盲读。** 现在第三读者的提示词开头就写着\"The library has filed 'later' in the group of 'earlier' as a repeat\"（`clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/merge-third-prompt.md:3`），等于把系统的判定告诉了读者。比较两组的分歧时，必须改用中性提问。代价是和以往第 2 条线的读法不能完全对齐。\n- **\"条件信息\"同样只是假设。** 分数比 Jev 已看到的文本多出来的，只有两样：上面说的那两个字段，以及另一个模型对相似度的看法。即使真分数组胜出，没有 X 组也说不清功劳该归谁。\n- **候选固定的重发只测比较这一步，也证明不了能上生产。** 真实运行中，一次判定改变后，后面记录的候选也会跟着变。\n\n---\n\n## 2. 有什么证据，缺什么证据\n\n| 问题 | 状态 | 依据 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 现在分数没有交给 Jev | **证实** | `compare.py:100-106`、`:132-136` |\n| clean 路径从没测过把分数给 Jev | **在搜索范围内证实**：`clean-arch/**/*.py` 里 cosine 只用于检索；`tn-hivemind` 没搜 | `compare.py`、`retrieve.py`、`forward_sim.py`、`score_retrieval_v2.py` |\n| 存档里的请求就是当时发出的原始字节 | **证实**：发送和存档都用 `json.dumps(sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)`。这一点和生成式调用不同（AGENTS §5 的警告针对的是 `model.call`） | `jev.py:32`、`model.py:242`、`jev.py:89-90` |\n| 怎样避开缓存 | **证实**：按请求的 sha 查存档，用新的存档文件就不会命中；返回结果的 `cached` 字段可以核对 | `jev.py:92-95` |\n| 候选顺序和问题 id 一一对应，并已存下 | **证实** | `compare.py:132`、`:142`、`:147` |\n| c8 的验收集和 dev 三次都有完整存档 | **证实**：`jev.sqlite`、`decisions.json`、`embeddings.json` 都在；验收集还有读者对合并的判定 | `poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/`、`clean-step1-c8-dev-d{1,2,3}-2026-11-09/step2/` |\n| 不依赖 Jev 的已知重复 | **验收集有**：运行前定下 26 个重复组、82 个成员（`step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:1579`），已冻结。但不完整：只覆盖读者保留的事项，捆绑事项会同时出现在两组（`:1592`） | |\n| dev 的参考答案不完整 | **证实**：Jev 判成重复、但参考答案没标过的配对里，约一半其实是真重复 | `step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md:96-99` |\n| \"同时像好几个组\"的情况很常见 | **证实**：验收集 57 个重复里有 16 个；dev 三次分别是 13/100、25/100、11/106。选哪个组是分数可能起作用的一大块地方（这一点是假设） | 各次 `step2.log:2` |\n| Step 2 的分数分布、X4 的分数 | **没有** | 可以零成本算 |\n| Jev 会不会用、怎么用一个数字 | **没有** | 只有厂商 1.13 版的二手说法 |\n| 这种请求重发时 Jev 的随机波动 | **仓库里没有** | 只有厂商自己的例子（codex review `:104`） |\n| c8 上 Jev 漏判重复的比例 | **没测**：没有任何一条线测它 | 验收集可以对照运行前定下的重复组零成本数出来 |\n| 修订 | **几乎没覆盖** | 验收集 0 个，dev 每次 2–3 个 |\n\n---\n\n## 3. 能区分\"有益\"和\"有害\"的实验\n\n**数据：** 先只用 c8 验收集，188 条记录。dev 三次留到验收集出现信号之后再用。\n\n**各组请求（每条记录一个请求，候选、顺序、state、criteria、问题 id、模型全部不变）：**\n\n| 组 | 内容 | 用来回答什么 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **C**：原样 | 存档里的请求一字不改，发到一个新的存档文件 | 不命中缓存的对照。三次之间的分歧就是噪声底线 |\n| **T**：真分数 | 每个问题的 `instructions` 在旧证据文本之后加一行固定格式的分数。只说明分数从哪来（\"一个独立的检索模型算出的文本向量余弦\"），不说怎么用，不给门槛，不写\"越高越像\" | 有没有效果 |\n| **P**：打乱分数 | 格式和 T 一字不差。分数在同一请求的候选之间按每条查询分别打乱（固定种子），数字的集合和各查询的刻度都保留，但和候选的对应关系被打断 | T 的效果来自分数里的信息，还是只来自\"多了一行数字\" |\n| **X**（只有 T 优于 P 才做） | 不加分数，把 `evidence_period` 直接写进文本 | 分数是不是只在替 Jev 看不到的字段传话 |\n\n- **分数规则（应对多查询的歧义）：** 预先登记\"全部给出、逐条标明来源\"。例如：\"按论点'…?'检索：0.xxx；按本记录自身文本检索：0.yyy\"。每个组在每条查询下的分数其实都算过（`compare.py:104` 会给库里所有组打分），所以不存在缺失值。这样既回避了\"取最大值还是取最先找到的那条\"的选择，也不会把刻度不同的数字混成一个。P 组在每一列里各自打乱。只有一个候选、或者分数全部相同的请求没法打乱，单独报告。\n- **发送前的零成本检查：** 逐字节比对 T 和 C，只允许多出那几行；P 和 T 只允许数字不同。\n- **不命中缓存：** 每组每次用一个新的存档；所有返回的 `cached` 必须都是 False。厂商那边有没有缓存，文档没说，未知。\n- **时间混杂：** 三个组的请求打乱顺序交错发送，避免厂商在发送期间变动造成的差异。\n- **重复次数：** 每组 3 次。C 组内部三次之间的分歧，就是\"什么都不改也会变\"的基线。\n\n**分析（两层，性质不同）：**\n\n1. **Jev 用不用这个数字**：不需要标签，每个\"新证据—候选\"配对都能用，数据量大。\n   - 先算每个配对上 T 相对 C、P 相对 C 的 `same_statement` 概率变化。\n   - 在 P 组里，显示的数字和文本无关。如果概率变化仍然跟着这个数字走，说明 Jev 在跟数字走，而不管文本说什么，这本身就是一个风险信号。\n   - 在 T 组里，看变化是否超过 P 组和 C 组之间的噪声。\n   - 这一层是对敏感度的结构性测量，不是质量评分。质量的判定仍然靠人读原文。\n2. **是好是坏**：只读分歧的那部分。\n   - 用不变的 `compare.outcome` 算出每条记录在各组的结果：归入哪个组、修订、还是新记录。\n   - 两组之间有任何一次结果不同的记录，或者归入的组变了的记录，把相关配对去重后交给读者。\n   - 混入一部分各组结论一致的配对和已知答案的配对作为对照，让读者看不出\"这里每一对都有争议\"。\n   - 读者看不到分组、概率、分数和名次。\n   - 中性提问：后一条是否报告了前一条的主要陈述？可选 acceptable / overlap / 修订 / 不同事实。\n   - 提示词和判定流程在读之前冻结；两个读者，有分歧的交给第三个读者。完全相同的配对沿用以前的判定，和 §32 的做法一样（`LOG.md:1160`）。\n\n**判定逐条记录**：修好了（错误合并变成不合并、漏判变成正确合并、错的目标组变成对的）、改坏了（反方向）、中性。T 对 C、T 对 P、P 对 C、C 对 C 四组对比，结论按下表解读：\n\n| 观察 | 解读 |\n|---|---|\n| T、P、C 的分歧都只在 C 对 C 的噪声水平 | 在这个样本量下看不出效果。**不等于没有效果** |\n| T ≈ P，但都和 C 不同 | 变化来自多出的那行字，不来自分数信息，不能归功于分数 |\n| T 和 P 不同，T 修好的比 P 多，改坏的不比 P 多 | Jev 在利用分数信息，而且方向是好的。下一步在冻结的 c8 记录上做一次前向运行，用三条线判 |\n| T 改坏的多于修好的 | 有害证据 |\n\n- **门槛不在这里定**：比如\"三次里至少两次重现\"这类规则，要在发送前由 council 登记好。\n- **样本小，只能当线索**：每次运行只有 1–3 个错误合并，单看错误合并在统计上什么也证明不了。所以报告每一个案例和每一个数字，不做显著性的说法。\n- **漏判的重复**：在验收集上，以运行前定下的重复组为准，统计每组漏判了多少个已知重复，并读其中有分歧的那些。\n- **修订**：验收集一个都没有，这个实验测不到。如果需要，可以用 v2 参考答案里 25 对修订做配对级的重发（`step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md:93`）。但那不是产品真实的请求形状，必须这样标注。\n\n**成本（估算）：** Jev 的价格是每百万输入 token $0.042。早期一次完整前向运行约 $0.054（`step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md:192`），那时还没有用完整引文。验收集 3 组 × 3 次共 9 次重发，只算比较请求、不算事后挂载，估计不到 1 美元。确切数字可以先从 `jev.sqlite` 存的 token 数零成本算出。主要成本是读者时间，取决于分歧的数量，现在不知道。\n\n---\n\n## 4. 离线零成本分析的定位\n\n**它不是关卡，阴性结果也不是定论。** 两个方向都不成立：分布重叠不能说明没用，有区分度也不能说明 Jev 会用。它在发送前仍有四个用处：\n\n1. **估规模**：多少候选有不止一个查询分数；同一请求内分数的跨度有多大，跨度太小，T 和 P 就几乎无法区分；多少请求只有一个候选、没法打乱。\n2. **定格式**：给登记分数规则和打乱方法提供依据。\n3. **写预测**：发送前就写下哪些记录最可能翻转，让结果可以被证伪。\n4. **补标签**：分数高但参考答案没标的配对，可能是漏掉的重复。在任何一组发送之前就交给读者，这样不会受分组影响。\n\n**它唯一接近定论的情形**是同一请求内的分数几乎都一样。那时 T 和 P 在构造上就分不开，实验无法检验\"Jev 是否利用分数信息\"。即便如此，也只能说\"这个实验测不了\"，不能说\"没用\"。\n\n---\n\n- **本轮没做的：** 没有发送任何请求，没有算任何分数，没有改任何文件，也没有读另一位审查者对同一问题的输出。\n- **核查范围：** 读了 c8 验收集和 dev 三次的 Step 2 日志与目录清单、第三读者提示词、`model.request_identity`，以及 `CURRENT_STATE.md` 中的相关行。"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8055,"cache_read_input_tokens":226960,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8055},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c06c24f-8f77-4add-9443-7081a27b7903","uuid":"8cd85187-7df9-4814-97e5-a2edc0fed119","timestamp":"2026-11-09T01:05:56.443Z","request_id":"req_011CgrTKzvsY2EA9aCh7aGK8"}
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/round-2.jsonl:215:{"duration_api_ms":650043,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"4c06c24f-8f77-4add-9443-7081a27b7903","total_cost_usd":5.512593799999999,"usage":{"input_tokens":16,"cache_creation_input_tokens":244148,"cache_read_input_tokens":1521850,"output_tokens":25843,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":17883},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":244148,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"global","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":8896,"cache_read_input_tokens":226960,"cache_creation_input_tokens":8055,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":8055},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard","fallback_credit":null},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":58,"outputTokens":50314,"thinkingTokens":32982,"cacheReadInputTokens":4035049,"cacheCreationInputTokens":462384,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":5.512593799999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":14,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"# 把 cosine 交给 Jev：自我挑战与逐条回应（只读）\n\n**修正后的结论：上一轮我把\"离线分数分析没有区分度\"当成\"不必发送\"的理由，这是错的。** 离线分析既证明不了没用，也证明不了 Jev 会用这个分数。能真正回答问题的最便宜检验，是把已存的 Jev 请求原样重发，分成三组对照：\n\n- **原样组**：请求一字不改；\n- **真分数组**：只在每个问题里加上真实的分数；\n- **打乱分数组**：同一请求内把分数在候选之间打乱后加上。\n\n只在验收集上做，估计花费不到 1 美元（这是估算）；真正的成本是读者的时间。它改动了 Jev 的输入，所以算一轮新改动：发送前要过 council，并由 Alex 决定是否开这一轮。当前排在第一的任务是 D388（`docs/CURRENT_STATE.md:123-125`）。\n\n---\n\n## 1. 对你每一条的回应\n\n| # | 你的观点 | 我的立场 | 理由与证据 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | 分数的分布在两组之间重叠，Jev 照样可能受益（条件信息、交互作用）；单变量离线检验失败证明不了没好处；有区分度也证明不了 Jev 在用 | **同意，两半都同意** | 上一轮的\"A 步不通过就停\"不该当决策规则。补一个具体机制：分数里含有 Jev 现在看不到的信息。被向量化的文本 `doc_text` 里有 `evidence_period`，`query_text` 里有论点问题（`compare.py:31-37`），而 Jev 看到的 `piece_text` 两样都没有（`compare.py:40-42`）。所以\"条件信息\"在结构上确实存在。这也带来一个混杂因素：分数即使有用，也可能只是在替这两个字段传话，所以归因需要单独的对照（见第 3 节 X 组）。 |\n| 2a | \"0.4 已经算高、这个模型分数天然偏低\"来自另一个任务，不能推广 | **同意，撤回** | 依据 `search.py:27-30` 是 2026-10-24 在 74 句话上做的\"想法对观点\"任务，文本模板不同。我读过的所有文件里，都没有 Step 2 候选的分数分布。用缓存的向量可以零成本算出来，但现在没人算过。 |\n| 2b | 第 10 名的分数不一定高 | **同意，还要补一条** | `search()` 是把整个库排序后截前 10（`compare.py:104`）。前向运行的早期，库里不到 10 个组，所有组都会成为候选，和相似度无关。所以同一请求里分数的跨度，早期可能很大、后期可能很窄。这一点是读代码得出的；具体数值不知道。 |\n| 2c | 不知道 X4 的 cosine | **同意，撤回这个例子** | 我说\"它进前 10 正是因为 cosine 高\"是错的。进前 10 只说明它在当时的库里排名靠前，说明不了绝对数值。 |\n| 3 | 没发现 Step 2 的瓶颈、验收通过、1/57 贴近门槛，这些都不能说明影响，也不能说明可以上生产；数字有限 | **同意** | 我把两件事混在了一起。一件是排序：有没有一个正在失败的错误类型需要动手（AGENTS §1、§7.3）。另一件是分数本身有没有效果。前者说明不了后者。还要更正三处：(a) \"Search is not the bottleneck\"（`step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md:176`）说的是检索，不是比较；(b) 现有三条线都不测 Jev 漏判的重复；(c) 验收集里一个修订都没有（`clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2.log:2`，只有 new 和 repeat 两种结果），dev 每次也只有 2–3 个。1/57 的不确定性也很大：Clopper–Pearson 双侧 95% 上界约 9.4%（我的估算），所以\"达线\"只是点估计。\"只差一个合并\"说明的是这条线很脆弱，不是分数有害的证据。 |\n| 4 | 把 LLM 的锚定效应套到 Jev 上只是假设；Jev 不生成文字，是另一类东西；不能断言它不会推理、没有数字刻度 | **同意，撤回断言** | 能观察到的只有：它不返回文字，所以我们看不到它怎么推理。它内部会不会推理、能不能把数字当刻度来用，仓库里没有证据。厂商 1.13 版\"数字推理是弱项\"的说法，我是从 `codex-jev-usage-review.md:343` 二手转述的：版本是 1.13 不是 1.14，没有给数字，我也没读原页。\"分数会强化错误\"降级为三个并列假设之一：有帮助、有害、被忽略。 |\n| 5 | 离线分析有用，但不该当关卡；它的阴性结果算不算定论 | **同意：不是定论，也不当关卡** | AGENTS §1 第 4 步要求的\"最便宜的证明\"，原文就是\"a stored input edited and re-run\"，也就是改一个存储的输入再重发，而不是先做一次分数普查。离线分析的用处见第 4 节。 |\n\n**我仍然坚持、或者反过来挑战你的几点：**\n\n- **合并歧义是真实存在的（读代码证实）。** 一个候选对应几条查询就有几个分数（`compare.py:45-51`、`:103-105`）。给分数的规则必须在发送前登记好，否则真分数组本身就没有定义。\n- **只要改了 Jev 的输入，就是新的一轮。** 仓库里对另一处改动已经写过同样的原则：\"changing it changes measured Step 2 behaviour and needs its own measurement\"（`docs/CURRENT_STATE.md:37`）。加进去的那句话在判别标准里找不到出处，按 AGENTS §6 属于要交给 Alex 的提议。\n- **\"沿用同一套读者流程\"做不到完全盲读。** 现在第三读者的提示词开头就写着\"The library has filed 'later' in the group of 'earlier' as a repeat\"（`clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/merge-third-prompt.md:3`），等于把系统的判定告诉了读者。比较两组的分歧时，必须改用中性提问。代价是和以往第 2 条线的读法不能完全对齐。\n- **\"条件信息\"同样只是假设。** 分数比 Jev 已看到的文本多出来的，只有两样：上面说的那两个字段，以及另一个模型对相似度的看法。即使真分数组胜出，没有 X 组也说不清功劳该归谁。\n- **候选固定的重发只测比较这一步，也证明不了能上生产。** 真实运行中，一次判定改变后，后面记录的候选也会跟着变。\n\n---\n\n## 2. 有什么证据，缺什么证据\n\n| 问题 | 状态 | 依据 |\n|---|---|---|\n| 现在分数没有交给 Jev | **证实** | `compare.py:100-106`、`:132-136` |\n| clean 路径从没测过把分数给 Jev | **在搜索范围内证实**：`clean-arch/**/*.py` 里 cosine 只用于检索；`tn-hivemind` 没搜 | `compare.py`、`retrieve.py`、`forward_sim.py`、`score_retrieval_v2.py` |\n| 存档里的请求就是当时发出的原始字节 | **证实**：发送和存档都用 `json.dumps(sort_keys=True, ensure_ascii=False)`。这一点和生成式调用不同（AGENTS §5 的警告针对的是 `model.call`） | `jev.py:32`、`model.py:242`、`jev.py:89-90` |\n| 怎样避开缓存 | **证实**：按请求的 sha 查存档，用新的存档文件就不会命中；返回结果的 `cached` 字段可以核对 | `jev.py:92-95` |\n| 候选顺序和问题 id 一一对应，并已存下 | **证实** | `compare.py:132`、`:142`、`:147` |\n| c8 的验收集和 dev 三次都有完整存档 | **证实**：`jev.sqlite`、`decisions.json`、`embeddings.json` 都在；验收集还有读者对合并的判定 | `poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/`、`clean-step1-c8-dev-d{1,2,3}-2026-11-09/step2/` |\n| 不依赖 Jev 的已知重复 | **验收集有**：运行前定下 26 个重复组、82 个成员（`step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md:1579`），已冻结。但不完整：只覆盖读者保留的事项，捆绑事项会同时出现在两组（`:1592`） | |\n| dev 的参考答案不完整 | **证实**：Jev 判成重复、但参考答案没标过的配对里，约一半其实是真重复 | `step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md:96-99` |\n| \"同时像好几个组\"的情况很常见 | **证实**：验收集 57 个重复里有 16 个；dev 三次分别是 13/100、25/100、11/106。选哪个组是分数可能起作用的一大块地方（这一点是假设） | 各次 `step2.log:2` |\n| Step 2 的分数分布、X4 的分数 | **没有** | 可以零成本算 |\n| Jev 会不会用、怎么用一个数字 | **没有** | 只有厂商 1.13 版的二手说法 |\n| 这种请求重发时 Jev 的随机波动 | **仓库里没有** | 只有厂商自己的例子（codex review `:104`） |\n| c8 上 Jev 漏判重复的比例 | **没测**：没有任何一条线测它 | 验收集可以对照运行前定下的重复组零成本数出来 |\n| 修订 | **几乎没覆盖** | 验收集 0 个，dev 每次 2–3 个 |\n\n---\n\n## 3. 能区分\"有益\"和\"有害\"的实验\n\n**数据：** 先只用 c8 验收集，188 条记录。dev 三次留到验收集出现信号之后再用。\n\n**各组请求（每条记录一个请求，候选、顺序、state、criteria、问题 id、模型全部不变）：**\n\n| 组 | 内容 | 用来回答什么 |\n|---|---|---|\n| **C**：原样 | 存档里的请求一字不改，发到一个新的存档文件 | 不命中缓存的对照。三次之间的分歧就是噪声底线 |\n| **T**：真分数 | 每个问题的 `instructions` 在旧证据文本之后加一行固定格式的分数。只说明分数从哪来（\"一个独立的检索模型算出的文本向量余弦\"），不说怎么用，不给门槛，不写\"越高越像\" | 有没有效果 |\n| **P**：打乱分数 | 格式和 T 一字不差。分数在同一请求的候选之间按每条查询分别打乱（固定种子），数字的集合和各查询的刻度都保留，但和候选的对应关系被打断 | T 的效果来自分数里的信息，还是只来自\"多了一行数字\" |\n| **X**（只有 T 优于 P 才做） | 不加分数，把 `evidence_period` 直接写进文本 | 分数是不是只在替 Jev 看不到的字段传话 |\n\n- **分数规则（应对多查询的歧义）：** 预先登记\"全部给出、逐条标明来源\"。例如：\"按论点'…?'检索：0.xxx；按本记录自身文本检索：0.yyy\"。每个组在每条查询下的分数其实都算过（`compare.py:104` 会给库里所有组打分），所以不存在缺失值。这样既回避了\"取最大值还是取最先找到的那条\"的选择，也不会把刻度不同的数字混成一个。P 组在每一列里各自打乱。只有一个候选、或者分数全部相同的请求没法打乱，单独报告。\n- **发送前的零成本检查：** 逐字节比对 T 和 C，只允许多出那几行；P 和 T 只允许数字不同。\n- **不命中缓存：** 每组每次用一个新的存档；所有返回的 `cached` 必须都是 False。厂商那边有没有缓存，文档没说，未知。\n- **时间混杂：** 三个组的请求打乱顺序交错发送，避免厂商在发送期间变动造成的差异。\n- **重复次数：** 每组 3 次。C 组内部三次之间的分歧，就是\"什么都不改也会变\"的基线。\n\n**分析（两层，性质不同）：**\n\n1. **Jev 用不用这个数字**：不需要标签，每个\"新证据—候选\"配对都能用，数据量大。\n   - 先算每个配对上 T 相对 C、P 相对 C 的 `same_statement` 概率变化。\n   - 在 P 组里，显示的数字和文本无关。如果概率变化仍然跟着这个数字走，说明 Jev 在跟数字走，而不管文本说什么，这本身就是一个风险信号。\n   - 在 T 组里，看变化是否超过 P 组和 C 组之间的噪声。\n   - 这一层是对敏感度的结构性测量，不是质量评分。质量的判定仍然靠人读原文。\n2. **是好是坏**：只读分歧的那部分。\n   - 用不变的 `compare.outcome` 算出每条记录在各组的结果：归入哪个组、修订、还是新记录。\n   - 两组之间有任何一次结果不同的记录，或者归入的组变了的记录，把相关配对去重后交给读者。\n   - 混入一部分各组结论一致的配对和已知答案的配对作为对照，让读者看不出\"这里每一对都有争议\"。\n   - 读者看不到分组、概率、分数和名次。\n   - 中性提问：后一条是否报告了前一条的主要陈述？可选 acceptable / overlap / 修订 / 不同事实。\n   - 提示词和判定流程在读之前冻结；两个读者，有分歧的交给第三个读者。完全相同的配对沿用以前的判定，和 §32 的做法一样（`LOG.md:1160`）。\n\n**判定逐条记录**：修好了（错误合并变成不合并、漏判变成正确合并、错的目标组变成对的）、改坏了（反方向）、中性。T 对 C、T 对 P、P 对 C、C 对 C 四组对比，结论按下表解读：\n\n| 观察 | 解读 |\n|---|---|\n| T、P、C 的分歧都只在 C 对 C 的噪声水平 | 在这个样本量下看不出效果。**不等于没有效果** |\n| T ≈ P，但都和 C 不同 | 变化来自多出的那行字，不来自分数信息，不能归功于分数 |\n| T 和 P 不同，T 修好的比 P 多，改坏的不比 P 多 | Jev 在利用分数信息，而且方向是好的。下一步在冻结的 c8 记录上做一次前向运行，用三条线判 |\n| T 改坏的多于修好的 | 有害证据 |\n\n- **门槛不在这里定**：比如\"三次里至少两次重现\"这类规则，要在发送前由 council 登记好。\n- **样本小，只能当线索**：每次运行只有 1–3 个错误合并，单看错误合并在统计上什么也证明不了。所以报告每一个案例和每一个数字，不做显著性的说法。\n- **漏判的重复**：在验收集上，以运行前定下的重复组为准，统计每组漏判了多少个已知重复，并读其中有分歧的那些。\n- **修订**：验收集一个都没有，这个实验测不到。如果需要，可以用 v2 参考答案里 25 对修订做配对级的重发（`step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md:93`）。但那不是产品真实的请求形状，必须这样标注。\n\n**成本（估算）：** Jev 的价格是每百万输入 token $0.042。早期一次完整前向运行约 $0.054（`step2-validation-2026-11-07/LOG.md:192`），那时还没有用完整引文。验收集 3 组 × 3 次共 9 次重发，只算比较请求、不算事后挂载，估计不到 1 美元。确切数字可以先从 `jev.sqlite` 存的 token 数零成本算出。主要成本是读者时间，取决于分歧的数量，现在不知道。\n\n---\n\n## 4. 离线零成本分析的定位\n\n**它不是关卡，阴性结果也不是定论。** 两个方向都不成立：分布重叠不能说明没用，有区分度也不能说明 Jev 会用。它在发送前仍有四个用处：\n\n1. **估规模**：多少候选有不止一个查询分数；同一请求内分数的跨度有多大，跨度太小，T 和 P 就几乎无法区分；多少请求只有一个候选、没法打乱。\n2. **定格式**：给登记分数规则和打乱方法提供依据。\n3. **写预测**：发送前就写下哪些记录最可能翻转，让结果可以被证伪。\n4. **补标签**：分数高但参考答案没标的配对，可能是漏掉的重复。在任何一组发送之前就交给读者，这样不会受分组影响。\n\n**它唯一接近定论的情形**是同一请求内的分数几乎都一样。那时 T 和 P 在构造上就分不开，实验无法检验\"Jev 是否利用分数信息\"。即便如此，也只能说\"这个实验测不了\"，不能说\"没用\"。\n\n---\n\n- **本轮没做的：** 没有发送任何请求，没有算任何分数，没有改任何文件，也没有读另一位审查者对同一问题的输出。\n- **核查范围：** 读了 c8 验收集和 dev 三次的 Step 2 日志与目录清单、第三读者提示词、`model.request_identity`，以及 `CURRENT_STATE.md` 中的相关行。","ttft_ms":90388,"type":"result","duration_ms":325450,"uuid":"f1e6bb6c-08fb-477a-a457-3768ca00b08d","ttft_stream_ms":7371,"time_to_request_ms":367,"first_content_frame_ms":7372,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/harness-review-3.stderr:67:     3	Alex asks whether sending embedding similarity to Jev helps, given existing high retrieval recall and merge quality. This is an isolated fixed-history diagnostic, not a product change, adoption, a fresh held-out acceptance, or a comparison of search recall. Prior recorded acceptance 141/143 is search recall, 1/57 clearly wrong merges is not recall of Jev's repeat decisions. The fresh frozen reference and old labels do not change. Start with 11 archived c8 fresh comparison requests, selected before sending, covering the clearly wrong merge, disputed overlaps, accepted repeats, and new-evidence controls: `22:ev-11`, `13:e11`, `38:ev-2`, `18:e2`, `43:e3`, `3:e1`, `9:e6`, `14:e3`, `5:e1`, `9:e1`, `19:ev-guidance-70`. Two arms times three draws = 66 calls, with the original candidate sets and state fixed. This is a selected diagnostic and cannot measure overall precision or recall. A larger comparison is considered only if the cheap probe reveals a useful signal (AGENTS §7.3); the raw articles are already used, so neither probe is fresh acceptance.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/harness-review-3.stderr:111:    47	1. Report every request, candidate, transport failure, cost and baseline variability. Quantify disagreements C vs T and change in wrong merges, missed repeats, revisions and target group, by request, comparing the three draws in each arm. Score-sensitivity is not proof of accuracy. No search recall improvement can be attributed to this intervention because search is held fixed.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/harness-review-3.stderr:122:    58	Hypothesis: score information moves at least one relevant comparison and makes at least one source-backed decision better without a source-backed decision getting worse. Prediction: the clearly wrong X22 grouping becomes separate more often in T than C, while the selected accepted-repeat controls remain correctly grouped. We do not predict a perfect result. Predeclare individual decision comparisons, 3 samples per arm and show all 66 outcomes and errors. For each outcome and selected source-backed candidate, count correct and incorrect choices across three draws per arm. A repeatable improvement requires at least one agreed previously incorrect decision to become correct in at least 2 of 3 T draws and fewer than 2 of 3 C draws, with no agreed previously correct decision becoming wrong in at least 2 of 3 T draws while correct in at least 2 of 3 C draws. A repeatable regression stops the line. If neither occurs or independent readers disagree, report inconclusive. This is a screening rule for selected examples, not a quantitative estimate of product impact. Blind-read all eleven incoming records against all their candidate sets and source articles, including unchanged controls; report gaps. Register case ids and score mapping and historical top-ten replay before any send; send no paid calls until council review and preflight pass.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/harness-review-3.stderr:126:    62	The read-only Codex reviewer cleared harness design but not sending. Claude reviewed the earlier 10-case/three-arm draft and found lack of revision coverage, unsupported X22 direction and number presentation ambiguity; an eleventh recorded revision-bearing case was added. Its conclusion that 40 borderline probabilities bound opportunity is a hypothesis; confident outputs can also be wrong. The X22 prediction is a falsifiable probe hypothesis, not evidence of likely improvement. The shuffled arm is removed due to false attribution; C versus T assesses the total intervention, not score causation.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/harness-review-3.stderr:273:     9	SOURCE=ROOT/'poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09'; STEP=SOURCE/'step2';IDS=['22:ev-11','13:e11','38:ev-2','18:e2','43:e3','3:e1','9:e6','14:e3','5:e1','9:e1','19:ev-guidance-70']
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/codex-review.stderr:163:- Step 2 exploratory retrieval on 282 items found about 90% of reference targets at top-10 using thesis+evidence embeddings, 95.9% evidence-only, versus 82.1% production lexical retrieval. Only three cross-thesis positives were available. Forward simulation yielded 180 records, 102 merges, roughly two clear wrong merges plus six arguable and 14 missed repeats. [Task 1]
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/codex-review.stderr:476:reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/round-1.jsonl:40:{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Tn1pyarmYA5KWGY1Q6pQjq","type":"tool_result","content":"1603\t## 43. Acceptance on the fresh set: every line met; links are the weak point (2026-11-09)\n1604\t\n1605\tThe fresh Step 1 run finished: 50 of 50 articles complete in 52 calls. Two format failures were resent once and passed; in one of\n1606\tthem the model had added a field the schema does not have.\n1607\t- Cost: $0.66 at published rates (input $0.3/M, output $1.2/M, no cache share applied).\n1608\t- 188 kept items and 10 opened theses.\n1609\t- Step 2 placed the 188 records in 131 groups (57 repeats, 0 refused). Later linking judged 182 pairs and linked 1.\n1610\t\n1611\t**Readers.** Two readers per batch of ten articles, and a third reader on the 23 disputes (8 matters, 15 links). On the two articles\n1612\tI had traced myself (9 and 42) the readers agree with me.\n1613\t\n1614\t| Line | Result | Pass |\n1615\t|---|---|---|\n1616\t| Helpful matters kept | 132 / 139 = **95.0%** (core 83 / 83). All 7 misses are supporting: two author estimates, Huang's agent-compute claim (kept in another article), the capital-return policy, a driver exploit report, handheld openness, a Kioxia SSD | ≥ 81.2%: **met** |\n1617\t| Wrongly opened theses | **1** of 10, by both readers: clean-5, \"will Vera Rubin account for about 20% of data-center revenue in fiscal Q3\", a revenue share and so a financial measure (D382) | ≤ 2: **met** |\n1618\t| Search | **141 / 143** settled repeat pairs = 98.6%; 2 pairs not exercised because a member was not kept | ≥ 90%: **met** |\n1619\t| Wrong merges | **1 / 57** = 1.8%, none unjudged. 52 were accepted by both readers; of the 5 disputed, the third reader found 2 acceptable, 2 overlap and 1 wrong (Vera Rubin deliveries merged into production status and revenue share) | ≤ 2%: **met** |\n1620\t| Detail retention | grouped **22 / 26** = ungrouped 22 / 26. This is structural: all 188 records are stored with their own text. The 4 details missing are Step 1 omissions | no fewer: **met** |\n1621\t\n1622\t**My disagreement with the readers on theses.** I would also call two theses wrong:\n1623\t- clean-9, global semiconductor revenue in 2026 (Deloitte's estimate): an industry aggregate that adds little beyond NVIDIA's own\n1624\t  guidance;\n1625\t- clean-10, NAND demand created by NVIDIA's CMX: a memory supplier's quantity.\n1626\t\n1627\tBoth readers judged them shared quantities that the standard allows. By my reading the count is 3, which misses the line. This is\n1628\treported both ways.\n1629\t\n1630\t**Reported without a line.**\n1631\t- **Kept items.** Both readers called 138 helpful, 20 noise and 13 optional; the rest were split.\n1632\t- **Links: 59 / 93 judged right (63%).** This is the weak point. I read all 34 links that were not judged right:\n1633\t  - about 25 are real errors, where an item is linked to the topically nearest open thesis without bearing on its question. Examples:\n1634\t    SK Hynix's Indiana plant linked to NVIDIA's supplier commitments; a Fed-cut probability linked to hyperscaler capex; Wistron's\n1635\t    share sale linked to Vera Rubin's revenue share; Micron's revenue linked to NVIDIA's commitments;\n1636\t  - about 9 look like reader strictness. Examples: the acquisition announcement that founded the Hugging Face thesis; memory-cost\n1637\t    margin pressure linked to the server DRAM price thesis.\n1638\t- **The class in production.** It is production's open defect 1, where news is filed under the nearest revenue question (D355),\n1639\t  and the later-link disagreement of §41.\n1640\t\n1641\t**Next class (for the council):** link precision. First, a $0 check on the dev draws:\n1642\t- links per item and the share of items linked to two or more theses, c8 against c7;\n1643\t- whether c8's \"link one statement to every thesis it informs\" (an audit amendment) raised over-linking.\n1644\t\n1645\t## 44. Dev ×3, the reflection council, and the link recheck (2026-11-09)\n1646\t\n1647\t**Dev ×3 of the frozen c8** (115 dev articles, an empty start, each draw complete: 116, 115 and 117 calls; frozen golden-v5 dev,\n1648\tsha `6f9476bb…`, scored as a lead):\n1649\t\n1650\t| Measure | Draw 1 | Draw 2 | Draw 3 | c7 (earlier) |\n1651\t|---|---|---|---|---|\n1652\t| Helpful, of 234 (line 190) | 214 | 211 | 212 | 212 |\n1653\t| Core, of 86 | 85 | 86 | 86 | 86 |\n1654\t| Not-kept spans kept | 27 | 27 | 30 | 30 |\n1655\t| Theses opened | 8 | 10 | 10 | 10 |\n1656\t| must_open / may_open / none / must_not (one reader) | 4/3/1/0 | 3/3/3/1 (lidar) | 3/2/5/0 | 4/2/3/1 |\n1657\t| must_open covered, of 28 | 25 | 24 | 27 | 27 |\n1658\t| Search (reference mapped onto the draw) | 98/99 = 99.0% | 91/92 = 98.9% | 97/97 = 100% | |\n1659\t| Clear wrong merges (third reader) | 1/100 | 1/100 | 1/106 | |\n1660\t| Overlaps | 14 | 12 | 15 | |\n1661\t\n1662\t- **Stable across the three draws:** the six core theses (credit support, Vera Rubin, China H200, hyperscaler capex, Kyber, supply\n1663\t  commitments).\n1664\t- **Varies:** the edges (memory prices, Rubin Ultra, China budget shift, lidar, DeepSeek inquiry, custom ASIC pool, inference-chip\n1665\t  startups).\n1666\t- **Not covered in any draw:** the Ohio-guarantee yes/no question. The broader credit-support amount thesis is opened instead.\n1667\t\n1668\t**Reflection council** (a fresh thread, `council/ap-codex.md`, then `aq-codex.md`). It confirmed helpful, search and theses. It\n1669\tretracted its first claim of 3/57 wrong merges after reading the third reader's prompt: `merge_acceptable: false` is forced on\n1670\toverlaps, which the prompt defines as \"not misleading\", and the agreed line is clear wrong merges (D381). Agreed caveats:\n1671\t- report search both ways: 141/143 for search alone, 141/145 (97.2%) for the whole system. One 11-member group supplies 55 pairs, and\n1672\t  revisions are barely exercised;\n1673\t- line 3 is a storage comparison, not a usability test;\n1674\t- my thesis dissent is recorded as a breadth concern, not a count: the council reads clean-9 and clean-10 as supported shared\n1675\t  quantities;\n1676\t- c8 did not raise links per item, but that says nothing about whether the links are right.\n1677\t\n1678\tVerdict: REPORT AS STATED.\n1679\t\n1680\t**Link recheck (the council's cheapest next step).** A fresh senior-analyst reader saw the 34 links not judged right, mixed blind\n1681\twith 10 links judged right, and asked whether the item helps assess the question:\n1682\t\n1683\t| Original verdict | Useful | Weak | Wrong |\n1684\t|---|---|---|---|\n1685\t| Not right (34) | 13 | 19 | 2 |\n1686\t| Right, as controls (10) | 10 | 0 | 0 |\n1687\t\n1688\tOver all 93 links, about 72 are useful (77%), 19 are weak (20%: related, but they would not change the view) and 2 are wrong (2%).\n1689\tThe link problem is mainly clutter, not misleading filing. My earlier estimate of 25 real errors is withdrawn.\n1690\t\n1691\t**Next, for Alex:**\n1692\t- whether to adopt c8 as the clean Step 1 configuration (PRD §12);\n1693\t- whether link clutter, about one link in five, is worth a round. If it is, the round starts with the model's own account on weak\n1694\t  links, a few cents, before any design.\n1695\t\n1696\t## 45. Alex adopts c8 (D387); the PRD carries it; next, the account of weak links (2026-11-09)\n1697\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4c06c24f-8f77-4add-9443-7081a27b7903","uuid":"2c2ad6f9-4b05-4544-84f8-5283f6e5411e","timestamp":"2026-11-09T00:55:21.631Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/clean-arch/step1-unfiled-2026-11-08/LOG.md","content":"## 43. Acceptance on the fresh set: every line met; links are the weak point (2026-11-09)\n\nThe fresh Step 1 run finished: 50 of 50 articles complete in 52 calls. Two format failures were resent once and passed; in one of\nthem the model had added a field the schema does not have.\n- Cost: $0.66 at published rates (input $0.3/M, output $1.2/M, no cache share applied).\n- 188 kept items and 10 opened theses.\n- Step 2 placed the 188 records in 131 groups (57 repeats, 0 refused). Later linking judged 182 pairs and linked 1.\n\n**Readers.** Two readers per batch of ten articles, and a third reader on the 23 disputes (8 matters, 15 links). On the two articles\nI had traced myself (9 and 42) the readers agree with me.\n\n| Line | Result | Pass |\n|---|---|---|\n| Helpful matters kept | 132 / 139 = **95.0%** (core 83 / 83). All 7 misses are supporting: two author estimates, Huang's agent-compute claim (kept in another article), the capital-return policy, a driver exploit report, handheld openness, a Kioxia SSD | ≥ 81.2%: **met** |\n| Wrongly opened theses | **1** of 10, by both readers: clean-5, \"will Vera Rubin account for about 20% of data-center revenue in fiscal Q3\", a revenue share and so a financial measure (D382) | ≤ 2: **met** |\n| Search | **141 / 143** settled repeat pairs = 98.6%; 2 pairs not exercised because a member was not kept | ≥ 90%: **met** |\n| Wrong merges | **1 / 57** = 1.8%, none unjudged. 52 were accepted by both readers; of the 5 disputed, the third reader found 2 acceptable, 2 overlap and 1 wrong (Vera Rubin deliveries merged into production status and revenue share) | ≤ 2%: **met** |\n| Detail retention | grouped **22 / 26** = ungrouped 22 / 26. This is structural: all 188 records are stored with their own text. The 4 details missing are Step 1 omissions | no fewer: **met** |\n\n**My disagreement with the readers on theses.** I would also call two theses wrong:\n- clean-9, global semiconductor revenue in 2026 (Deloitte's estimate): an industry aggregate that adds little beyond NVIDIA's own\n  guidance;\n- clean-10, NAND demand created by NVIDIA's CMX: a memory supplier's quantity.\n\nBoth readers judged them shared quantities that the standard allows. By my reading the count is 3, which misses the line. This is\nreported both ways.\n\n**Reported without a line.**\n- **Kept items.** Both readers called 138 helpful, 20 noise and 13 optional; the rest were split.\n- **Links: 59 / 93 judged right (63%).** This is the weak point. I read all 34 links that were not judged right:\n  - about 25 are real errors, where an item is linked to the topically nearest open thesis without bearing on its question. Examples:\n    SK Hynix's Indiana plant linked to NVIDIA's supplier commitments; a Fed-cut probability linked to hyperscaler capex; Wistron's\n    share sale linked to Vera Rubin's revenue share; Micron's revenue linked to NVIDIA's commitments;\n  - about 9 look like reader strictness. Examples: the acquisition announcement that founded the Hugging Face thesis; memory-cost\n    margin pressure linked to the server DRAM price thesis.\n- **The class in production.** It is production's open defect 1, where news is filed under the nearest revenue question (D355),\n  and the later-link disagreement of §41.\n\n**Next class (for the council):** link precision. First, a $0 check on the dev draws:\n- links per item and the share of items linked to two or more theses, c8 against c7;\n- whether c8's \"link one statement to every thesis it informs\" (an audit amendment) raised over-linking.\n\n## 44. Dev ×3, the reflection council, and the link recheck (2026-11-09)\n\n**Dev ×3 of the frozen c8** (115 dev articles, an empty start, each draw complete: 116, 115 and 117 calls; frozen golden-v5 dev,\nsha `6f9476bb…`, scored as a lead):\n\n| Measure | Draw 1 | Draw 2 | Draw 3 | c7 (earlier) |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Helpful, of 234 (line 190) | 214 | 211 | 212 | 212 |\n| Core, of 86 | 85 | 86 | 86 | 86 |\n| Not-kept spans kept | 27 | 27 | 30 | 30 |\n| Theses opened | 8 | 10 | 10 | 10 |\n| must_open / may_open / none / must_not (one reader) | 4/3/1/0 | 3/3/3/1 (lidar) | 3/2/5/0 | 4/2/3/1 |\n| must_open covered, of 28 | 25 | 24 | 27 | 27 |\n| Search (reference mapped onto the draw) | 98/99 = 99.0% | 91/92 = 98.9% | 97/97 = 100% | |\n| Clear wrong merges (third reader) | 1/100 | 1/100 | 1/106 | |\n| Overlaps | 14 | 12 | 15 | |\n\n- **Stable across the three draws:** the six core theses (credit support, Vera Rubin, China H200, hyperscaler capex, Kyber, supply\n  commitments).\n- **Varies:** the edges (memory prices, Rubin Ultra, China budget shift, lidar, DeepSeek inquiry, custom ASIC pool, inference-chip\n  startups).\n- **Not covered in any draw:** the Ohio-guarantee yes/no question. The broader credit-support amount thesis is opened instead.\n\n**Reflection council** (a fresh thread, `council/ap-codex.md`, then `aq-codex.md`). It confirmed helpful, search and theses. It\nretracted its first claim of 3/57 wrong merges after reading the third reader's prompt: `merge_acceptable: false` is forced on\noverlaps, which the prompt defines as \"not misleading\", and the agreed line is clear wrong merges (D381). Agreed caveats:\n- report search both ways: 141/143 for search alone, 141/145 (97.2%) for the whole system. One 11-member group supplies 55 pairs, and\n  revisions are barely exercised;\n- line 3 is a storage comparison, not a usability test;\n- my thesis dissent is recorded as a breadth concern, not a count: the council reads clean-9 and clean-10 as supported shared\n  quantities;\n- c8 did not raise links per item, but that says nothing about whether the links are right.\n\nVerdict: REPORT AS STATED.\n\n**Link recheck (the council's cheapest next step).** A fresh senior-analyst reader saw the 34 links not judged right, mixed blind\nwith 10 links judged right, and asked whether the item helps assess the question:\n\n| Original verdict | Useful | Weak | Wrong |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Not right (34) | 13 | 19 | 2 |\n| Right, as controls (10) | 10 | 0 | 0 |\n\nOver all 93 links, about 72 are useful (77%), 19 are weak (20%: related, but they would not change the view) and 2 are wrong (2%).\nThe link problem is mainly clutter, not misleading filing. My earlier estimate of 25 real errors is withdrawn.\n\n**Next, for Alex:**\n- whether to adopt c8 as the clean Step 1 configuration (PRD §12);\n- whether link clutter, about one link in five, is worth a round. If it is, the round starts with the model's own account on weak\n  links, a few cents, before any design.\n\n## 45. Alex adopts c8 (D387); the PRD carries it; next, the account of weak links (2026-11-09)\n","numLines":95,"startLine":1603,"totalLines":2286}}}
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/codex-review.stderr:483:     3	Alex asks whether sending embedding similarity to Jev helps, given existing high retrieval recall and merge quality. This is an isolated fixed-history diagnostic, not a product change, adoption, a fresh held-out acceptance, or a comparison of search recall. Prior recorded acceptance 141/143 is search recall, 1/57 clearly wrong merges is not recall of Jev's repeat decisions. The fresh frozen reference and old labels do not change. Start with 10 archived c8 fresh comparison requests, selected before sending, covering the clearly wrong merge, disputed overlaps, accepted repeats, and new-evidence controls: `22:ev-11`, `13:e11`, `38:ev-2`, `18:e2`, `43:e3`, `3:e1`, `9:e6`, `14:e3`, `5:e1`, `9:e1`. Three arms times three draws = 90 calls, with the original candidate sets and state fixed. This is a selected diagnostic and cannot measure overall precision or recall. A larger comparison is considered only if the cheap probe reveals a useful signal (AGENTS §7.3); the raw articles are already used, so neither probe is fresh acceptance.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/codex-review.stderr:527:    47	1. Report every request, candidate, transport failure, cost and baseline variability. Quantify disagreements C vs T vs P and change in wrong merges, missed repeats, revisions and target group, paired by request and draw. Score-sensitivity is not proof of accuracy. No search recall improvement can be attributed to this intervention because search is held fixed.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/codex-review.stderr:528:    48	2. As Jev and saved references are incomplete, blind readers inspect all cases with changed outcomes and a predeclared random set of unchanged controls, including all known wrong merges and known-repeat candidates, against original sources. Mixed arms shown without scores, arm labels, candidate rank or model decision. Two independent reviews and adjudication of disagreements; do not use a new score program as semantic judge. If workload exceeds available reviewer context, partition into bounded batches and report coverage.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/codex-review.stderr:538:    58	Hypothesis: score information moves at least one relevant comparison beyond the change caused by a shuffled number and makes at least one source-backed decision better without a source-backed decision getting worse. Prediction: the clearly wrong X22 grouping becomes separate more often in T than C, while the selected accepted-repeat controls remain correctly grouped. We do not predict a perfect result. Predeclare individual decision comparisons, 3 samples per arm and show all 90 outcomes and errors. If T fails to improve any inspected decision, or causes a material wrong merge or loses a valid repeat without a balancing demonstrated gain, stop this line and report; no full experiment follows automatically. If a decisive contrast is absent or conflicting, report inconclusive. This is a heuristic stop on the selected probe, not a quantitative estimate of product impact. Blind-read every differing case plus each selected known-merge reference and at least two unchanged controls, including all original source material. Register case ids and score mapping before any send; send no paid calls until council review and preflight pass.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/codex-review.stderr:963:     3	Alex asks whether sending embedding similarity to Jev helps, given existing high retrieval recall and merge quality. This is an isolated fixed-history diagnostic, not a product change, adoption, a fresh held-out acceptance, or a comparison of search recall. Prior recorded acceptance 141/143 is search recall, 1/57 clearly wrong merges is not recall of Jev's repeat decisions. The fresh frozen reference and old labels do not change. Start with 10 archived c8 fresh comparison requests, selected before sending, covering the clearly wrong merge, disputed overlaps, accepted repeats, and new-evidence controls: `22:ev-11`, `13:e11`, `38:ev-2`, `18:e2`, `43:e3`, `3:e1`, `9:e6`, `14:e3`, `5:e1`, `9:e1`. Three arms times three draws = 90 calls, with the original candidate sets and state fixed. This is a selected diagnostic and cannot measure overall precision or recall. A larger comparison is considered only if the cheap probe reveals a useful signal (AGENTS §7.3); the raw articles are already used, so neither probe is fresh acceptance.
