reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/codex-review.stderr:2525:For example, the known X22 error grouped a report of **commercial deliveries** with an earlier report about **production status and a revenue-share forecast**. Both original readers called those different facts. A useful probe must establish whether giving Jev the real search score improves that decision without causing other wrong groupings—and must not describe a shuffled score as though it were the real similarity. [Source packet]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/merge-packet-1.json:882), [reader verdicts]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/merge-third-answer.json:14).
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/codex-review.stderr:2541:4. **The decision and stopping rule are not yet executable.** The design says to “predeclare a compact decision before send,” but also leaves “material” harm and “balancing demonstrated gain” undefined. It predicts a better X22 result and no worsening of accepted repeats, yet permits balancing harm against gain. [Design]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/EXPERIMENT-DESIGN.md:50). Three stochastic draws do not have a natural one-to-one pairing across arms; a difference in individual draws alone does not establish a score effect.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/CONCLUSIONS.md:11:In saved c6 X4, incoming 12:e1 was grouped into 1:E1 although the two revenue-sharing arrangements were judged different. Recomputed from the cached exact-text vectors, cosine of the one thesis query against 1:E1's document is 0.8574. Its own document-vector cosine is 0.8654, but the record had one thesis query and that value was not its retrieval query. The saved Jev answer called same_statement at 0.89. This is one error; it neither establishes that score information will harm Jev nor measures a score distribution. Source: `poc/data/clean-step2-forward-c6-2026-11-08/{decisions.json,library.json,embeddings.json,merge-key.json,merge-third-answer.json}`. Query/doc text and cosine are reconstructed as `clean-arch/step2/compare.py` defines them.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/CONCLUSIONS.md:19:Reconstruct identical saved candidate requests; interleave fresh no-score controls with true-score requests and a score-shuffled control, with fixed score representation and randomization, repeated draws, cache misses, and identical model, candidates and question content except score lines. Make each score's query origin explicit: multiple search queries may yield different scores. A shuffled control tests sensitivity to a number but needs care with singleton/equal-score cases and preserving query origin. A source-blind independent reader judges differing pairs and controls without seeing arm, score, or prior decision. Report wrong merges, missed repeats, incorrect revision classifications and group choices separately, all cases, with same-arm variability, cost and limitations; fixed-candidate comparisons do not prove forward-run performance. The fresh set has few or no revisions; use separately identified stored revision cases without presenting isolated pair results as product-path evidence. Freeze design, audit and preflight under repository rules before any paid send. A score can also encode context Jev did not directly receive (e.g. thesis wording or period), so improvement would not itself establish the mechanism.
