reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/RESULTS.md:7:The seventh case's first dispatch (`18:e2`, treatment draw 1) failed with `ConnectionResetError` after 36 successful answers. Whether that request reached the service is unknown. Per the predeclared single-attempt stop rule it was not retried; 29 further planned calls were not sent. Six cases have all six answers; five cases have no complete paired result. In particular the known wrong merge (`22:ev-11`) and revision-bearing example (`19:ev-guidance-70`) were not reached. Six completed cases carry 46 candidate comparisons; control and treatment each have three decisions per candidate. Logged successful input tokens 136,590, logged cost $0.005742; the ambiguous request's actual billing is unknown.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/codex-review.out:3:For example, the known X22 error grouped a report of **commercial deliveries** with an earlier report about **production status and a revenue-share forecast**. Both original readers called those different facts. A useful probe must establish whether giving Jev the real search score improves that decision without causing other wrong groupings—and must not describe a shuffled score as though it were the real similarity. [Source packet]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/merge-packet-1.json:882), [reader verdicts]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/merge-third-answer.json:14).
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/codex-review.out:19:4. **The decision and stopping rule are not yet executable.** The design says to “predeclare a compact decision before send,” but also leaves “material” harm and “balancing demonstrated gain” undefined. It predicts a better X22 result and no worsening of accepted repeats, yet permits balancing harm against gain. [Design]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/EXPERIMENT-DESIGN.md:50). Three stochastic draws do not have a natural one-to-one pairing across arms; a difference in individual draws alone does not establish a score effect.
reports/step2-score-council-2026-11-08/codex-review.md:3:For example, the known X22 error grouped a report of **commercial deliveries** with an earlier report about **production status and a revenue-share forecast**. Both original readers called those different facts. A useful probe must establish whether giving Jev the real search score improves that decision without causing other wrong groupings—and must not describe a shuffled score as though it were the real similarity. [Source packet]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/merge-packet-1.json:882), [reader verdicts]( /Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/clean-acceptance-2026-11-09/step2/merge-third-answer.json:14).
